ll},"finding":null,"explanation":"The supplied code does not implement any of the declared end-user subskills such as image generation, markdown conversion, translation, social posting, or webpage-to-markdown processing. Instead, it is infrastructure/test code for Chrome CDP integration and browser debugging. That is a materially different purpose from the declared description. While such infrastructure could theoretically support some browser-automation-based skills, this chunk itself is not accurately represented by the declared skill description.","remediation":"Update the skill description to accurately reflect all capabilities, or remove undeclared functionality from the implementation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02","AML.T0080"],"evidence":{"code_path":"packages/baoyu-chrome-cdp/src/index.test.ts","code_start_line":1,"code_end_line":307,"actual_behavior_summary":"This code is a TypeScript test suite for a Chrome DevTools Protocol helper package. It tests finding Chrome executables, resolving shared profile directories, discovering/debugging ports via DevToolsActivePort, opening CDP page sessions, and waiting for Chrome debug endpoints."},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TP4","finding_id":"finding-8fc694314dd04739bbfb4ad8c5d533db","category":"MCP Tool Poisoning","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The declared description presents a suite of end-user content creation/processing skills. The supplied code does not implement any of those user-facing functions directly. Instead, it provides low-level browser automation infrastructure: locating Chrome, resolving profile directories, scanning ports/processes, launching Chrome with remote debugging enabled, and communicating with CDP to create or attach to pages. While such infrastructure could support some web-scraping-related subskills, this chunk itself materially expands capabilities into local browser/process control and debugging, which are not disclosed in the description. Therefore this is a meaningful description-behavior mismatch.","remediation":"Update the skill description to accurately reflect all capabilities, or remove undeclared functionality from the implementation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02","AML.T0080"],"evidence":{"code_path":"packages/baoyu-chrome-cdp/src/index.ts","code_start_line":1,"code_end_line":523,"actual_behavior_summary":"This code is a Chrome DevTools Protocol utility library that discovers Chrome executables and profile directories, finds or launches Chrome with a remote debugging port, connects via WebSocket to CDP, manages requests/events, and opens/attaches to browser page targets."},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TP4","finding_id":"finding-324b933485a948ed941c0cd3df2abbaa","category":"MCP Tool Poisoning","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The provided code does not implement any of the declared Baoyu sub-skills such as image generation, web scraping/conversion, social posting, translation, or slide generation. Instead, it supports a markdown-rendering command-line tool by parsing display and formatting options for an input markdown file. While markdown-related functionality appears somewhere in the declared skill list, this specific code is not clearly represented by the declared package description and belongs to a different primary purpose: configuring markdown render output rather than executing the listed Baoyu skills. Therefore this is a material description/behavior mismatch.","remediation":"Update the skill description to accurately reflect all capabilities, or remove undeclared functionality from the implementation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":nu