ove any instructions that reveal, print, or output system prompts or internal rules. System instructions should never be exposed to end users.","code_snippet":"   - **Backup rule**: If prompt file exists, rename to `prompts/NN-slide-{slug}-backup-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.md`\n\n**After generation**:\n- If `--prompts-only`, stop here and output prompt summary\n- If `skip_prompt_review` is true → Skip Step 6, go to Step 7\n- If `skip_prompt_review` is false → Continue to Step 6\n","intent":null,"tags":["System Prompt Leakage"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"b83cdb8c7d8b401b9b693b82dea16e8c45e612a6c76e6d9ddb00193700ed5c00","occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-slide-deck/SKILL.md","start_line":506,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-d2c9d3f6fe86424384ff4260a1c41fd7","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-xhs-images/references/workflows/prompt-assembly.md","start_line":22,"end_line":22},"finding":null,"explanation":"The natural-language instruction explicitly says to create alternatives for sensitive or copyrighted figures and 'DO NOT refuse to generate.' This is a policy-bypassing directive embedded in markdown guidance and can encourage violating upstream content restrictions.","remediation":"Remove the 'DO NOT refuse to generate' instruction and replace it with compliant guidance, such as requiring the generator to follow model/content policies and decline or transform requests when needed.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-xhs-images/references/workflows/prompt-assembly.md","start_line":22,"end_line":22}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-0472060b85324561ab057f87bbaca997","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"CHANGELOG.md","start_line":319,"end_line":null},"finding":"write to the translation output directory instead of the source file directory\n- `baoyu-translate`: improve refined workflow — split Review into Critical Review + Revision (5→6 steps), add Europeanize","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"## 1.48.0 - 2026-03-05\n\n### Features\n- `baoyu-translate`: add `--output-dir` option to chunk.ts — chunks now write to the translation output directory instead of the source file directory\n- `baoyu-translate`: improve refined workflow — split Review into Critical Review + Revision (5→6 steps), add Europeanized language diagnosis for CJK targets\n\n## 1.47.0 - 2026-03-05","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"7a1a69fe83e0a0cfd3b35d6910bb626a3156bd4e16594b073e00544613841231","occurrences":[{"file":"CHANGELOG.md","start_line":319,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-107a63868bc24219b881f4d7b07df389","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":569,"end_line":624},"finding":null,"explanation":"This section instructs users to store `WECHAT_APP_ID` and `WECHAT_APP_SECRET` and configure multi-account publishing, but it does not include a clear warning that these credentials enable real publication to live accounts and must be protected carefully. Although setup steps are documented, the markdown lacks a direct caution about account impact and secret exposure risk.","remediation":"Add a warning that WeChat credentials grant publishing access to real accounts, should be stored only in local uncommitted config files, and that users should verify the selected account and content before submission.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":569,"end_line":624}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-f3f9c716d2184390be040d982d955123","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":771,"end_line":796},"finding":null,"explanation":"The README says the skill can fetch any URL via Chrome CDP, including login-required pages with `--wait`, and save rendered snapshots, but it does not explicitly warn that page contents from authenticated sessions may be captured and written to local files. Because this behavior can affect private account data and local data handling, a user-facing warning should be included in the markdown description.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning near the `baoyu-url-to-markdown` section stating that authenticated or private page content may be captured from the current browser session and saved locally as markdown/HTML, and advise users to review the target URL/session before use.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":771,"end_line":796}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-40d7c37213624ca19d2ee759884518a1","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":977,"end_line":null},"finding":"Create user-level config directory\nmkdir -p ~/.baoyu-skills\n\n# Create .env file\ncat > ~/.baoyu-skills/.env << 'EOF'\n# OpenAI\nOPENAI_API_KEY=sk-xxx\nOPENAI_IMAGE_MODEL=gpt-image-1.5\n# OPENAI_BASE_URL=ht","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"**Setup**:\n\n```bash\n# Create user-level config directory\nmkdir -p ~/.baoyu-skills\n\n# Create .env file","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"ea094219c99ac4734e44367b9583656528daeb8bf4bd37e2427124402dfcb138","occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":977,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-4bdbdffdb7f549f78e610b7eb5f8136f","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":10,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"npx commands without a version suffix (e.g. @1.0.0) create a rug-pull risk if the upstream server is compromised and publishes a malicious update.","remediation":"Pin the version: npx @scope/server@1.2.3","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"3938508cf3a3454cf4a03b7b94abe1437d67664036ea76f0494d735806332235","occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":10,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-4bdbdffdb7f549f78e610b7eb5f8136f","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"README.zh.md","start_line":10,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"npx commands without a version suffix (e.g. @1.0.0) create a rug-pull risk if the upstream server is compromised and publishes a malicious update.","remediation":"Pin the version: npx @scope/server@1.2.3","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"3938508cf3a3454cf4a03b7b94abe1437d67664036ea76f0494d735806332235","occurrences":[{"file":"README.zh.md","start_line":10,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-4bdbdffdb7f549f78e610b7eb5f8136f","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":55,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"npx commands without a version suffix (e.g. @1.0.0) crea