ndefault_aspect: \"2.35:1\"  # 2.35:1|16:9|1:1\n\nquick_mode: false         # Skip confirmation when true\n\nlanguage: null            # zh|en|ja|ko|auto (null = auto-detect)\n","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"f2585ed1a9f8ffe69bade4f4a85869690c663180a11cc20f5d4a1c41371c139d","occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-cover-image/references/config/first-time-setup.md","start_line":143,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-ad4b243ef712445990aa109bc7cdaba4","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-cover-image/references/config/preferences-schema.md","start_line":31,"end_line":null},"finding":"Skip confirmation","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"\ndefault_aspect: \"2.35:1\"  # 2.35:1|16:9|1:1\n\nquick_mode: false         # Skip confirmation when true\n\nlanguage: null            # zh|en|ja|ko|auto (null = auto-detect)\n","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"f2585ed1a9f8ffe69bade4f4a85869690c663180a11cc20f5d4a1c41371c139d","occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-cover-image/references/config/preferences-schema.md","start_line":31,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-ad4b243ef712445990aa109bc7cdaba4","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-cover-image/references/config/preferences-schema.md","start_line":61,"end_line":null},"finding":"Skip confirmation","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"\ndefault_aspect: \"2.35:1\"  # 2.35:1|16:9|1:1\n\nquick_mode: false         # Skip confirmation when true\n\nlanguage: null            # zh|en|ja|ko|auto (null = auto-detect)\n","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"f2585ed1a9f8ffe69bade4f4a85869690c663180a11cc20f5d4a1c41371c139d","occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-cover-image/references/config/preferences-schema.md","start_line":61,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-549e7980f72d4de693fa2ab1d18f9bfc","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-cover-image/references/workflow/confirm-options.md","start_line":36,"end_line":36},"finding":null,"explanation":"The instruction states that language is auto-determined from input, saved preference, or source language and explicitly says there is no need to ask. This imposes a language/locale behavior without offering the user a choice or opt-in, which matches the policy-violation category for language or locale constraints.","remediation":"Allow the user to confirm or override the selected language, or document a justified and narrowly scoped locale constraint. For example, state that the detected language will be used by default but provide an explicit option to change it.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-cover-image/references/workflow/confirm-options.md","start_line":36,"end_line":36}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-1ea0e81565cb48f4a924ab5eafe796fc","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-cover-image/references/workflow/prompt-template.md","start_line":33,"end_line":33},"finding":null,"explanation":"The prompt template includes a mandatory `Language: [confirmed language]` field, and later instructs authors to 'Match confirmed language' without stating that the user must choose or opt into that language. This can violate language/locale policy if the skill forces output in a specific language by default rather than offering a choice.","remediation":"Clarify that language must be user-selected or inherited from explicit user preference/context, e.g. 'Language: [user-selected or source-matching language, unless user requests otherwise]'. Add a note that users may choose their preferred output language.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-cover-image/references/workflow/prompt-template.md","start_line":33,"end_line":33}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-54a6596ff9204252bb90144d9eb6f870","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-gemini-web/SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest description says to use this skill when other skills 'need image generation backend' or for 'vision-capable AI generation,' which is broader than a specific trigger phrase and lacks clear boundaries for when this skill should or should not activate. Because this is a manifest/markdown context, the vague scope could cause unintended invocation for many general generation requests.","remediation":"Restrict the trigger description to explicit, narrowly scoped phrases or contexts, and add exclusion examples. For example, list exact invocation phrases and clarify when other image or text-generation skills should be preferred instead.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-gemini-web/SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-7f18499305144222ada458a5a0dea5b1","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-gemini-web/SKILL.md","start_line":46,"end_line":null},"finding":"no consent","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"**Flow**:\n1. Check if consent file exists with `accepted: true` and `disclaimerVersion: \"1.0\"`\n2. If valid consent exists → print warning with `acceptedAt` date, proceed\n3. If no consent → show disclaimer, ask user via `AskUserQuestion`:\n   - \"Yes, I accept\" → create consent file with ISO timestamp, proceed\n   - \"No, I decline\" → output decline message, stop\n4. Consent file format: `{\"version\":1,\"accepted\":true,\"acceptedAt\":\"<ISO>\",\"disclaimerVersion\":\"1.0\"}`","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"4b9d13ac603b6b3b7223dbea83ec4db8a7d9cd4c5f75cb33027bd83f42ec46e4","occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-gemini-web/SKILL.md","start_line":46,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-3638672d0c964e46a070125ed37c798f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-gemini-web/SKILL.md","start_line":140,"end_line":143},"finding":null,"explanation":"The markdown explains that Google auth cookies are cached automatically and that an already-running local Chrome/Chromium debugging session may be reused, but it does not present this as a user-facing warning about privacy and account-impact risk. Under the markdown warning criteria, behavior affecting authentication state and browser session data should be explicitly disclosed as a caution.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning in the Authentication section that login cookies will be stored locally and that existing browser sessions may be reused unless a dedicated profile is specified. Recommend using --profile-dir or GEMINI_WEB_CHROME_PROFILE_DIR for isolation and explain the privacy implications.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-gemini-web/SKILL.md","start_line":140,"end_line":143}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-85c9d1f1922e4613a0bf672073638a7b","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-gemini-web/scripts/gemini-webapi/client.ts","start_line":161,"end_line":215},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest describes this subskill as 'Gemini网页抓取', which suggests page retrieval/scraping. This client not only fetches content from Gemini endpoints, but also refreshes authentication cookies in the background and writes updated cookies to disk, which is a materially broader behavior than mere web capture.","remediation":"Update the skill description to explicitly disclose authenticated Gemini session management and cookie persistence, or split credential/session handling into a separate clearly-scoped component.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-gemini-web/scripts/gemini-webapi/client.ts","start_line":161,"end_line":215}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-3a3d628802ab4bcb906813de0e5c87b0","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-gemini-web/scripts/gemini-webapi/client.ts","start_line":161,"end_line":161},"finding":null,"explanation":"This code writes the client's cookie set, including `__Secure-1PSID` and refreshed `__Secure-1PSIDTS`, to a local cookie file. The file contains no confirmation prompt, comment, or other user-facing disclosure explaining that sensitive session credentials will be stored on disk.","remediation":"Add a clear warning or comment/docstring disclosing that authentication cookies are persisted locally, and ideally provide an opt-in, configurable path, or a way to disable persistence.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-gemini-web/scripts/gemini-webapi/client.ts","start_line":161,"end_line":161}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-52b2b60846ac4be4a35aae67a3dcb844","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-gemini-web/scripts/gemini-webapi/client.ts","start_line":215,"end_line":215},"finding":null,"explanation":"During auto-refresh, the code updates `__Secure-1PSIDTS` and silently persists the refreshed cookie data again. This is a safety-relevant credential-handling operation, but the file provides no visible warning, prompt, or explanatory comment to inform users that credential material is being rewritten to local storage.","remediation":"Document this behavior near the auto-refresh logic and expose a user-visible option to disable or confirm credential persistence during refresh cycles.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-gemini-web/scripts/gemini-webapi/client.ts","start_line":215,"end_line":215}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-a2256e51144e4094a273db66dd42c039","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-gemini-web/scripts/gemini-webapi/components/gem-mixin.ts","start_line":171,"end_line":175},"finding":null,"explanation":"The delete_gem method issues a DELETE_GEM RPC call that removes a gem, but this file provides no confirmation prompt, user-facing log message, or explanatory comment/docstring warning that the operation is destructive. For a code-file audit under this rule, irreversible deletion without any disclosure is a missing user warning.","remediation":"Add a user-visible warning or confirmation step before deletion, or at minimum document the destructive behavior with a clear docstring/comment and ensure the skill's markdown documentation warns that this method permanently deletes a gem.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-gemini-web/scripts/gemini-webapi/components/gem-mixin.ts","start_line":171,"end_line":175}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-a19e9f9c602240dcb72af05805bf0772","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-gemini-web/scripts/gemini-webapi/types/image.ts","start_line":40,"end_line":40},"finding":null,"explanation":"This code attaches a Cookie header to outbound HTTP requests when cookies are provided, which can transmit session or authentication data to remote servers. The file contains no confirmation prompt, user-facing log, or explanatory comment/docstring warning that cookies may be sent during image download.","remediation":"Add a clear user-facing warning or confirmation before sending cookies, or document this behavior in code comments/docstrings and the skill README/SKILL.md. Consider logging when authenticated requests are made and limiting cookie use to trusted domains only.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-gemini-web/scripts/gemini-webapi/types/image.ts","start_line":40,"end_line":40}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-e6a0968d09154d78ba2affe0707f2e89","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.81,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-gemini-web/scripts/gemini-webapi/utils/cookie-file.ts","start_line":22,"end_line":61},"finding":null,"explanation":"This function reads and parses a local cookie file containing session/authentication values, which is access to sensitive credential material. There is no visible user disclosure, logging, comment, or docstring explaining that the skill accesses stored cookies from disk.","remediation":"Document and disclose that the skill reads locally stored cookies/session data, including the file location and purpose. Add a comment, docstring, or user-visible notice so users understand that sensitive authentication data is being accessed.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-gemini-web/scripts/gemini-webapi/utils/cookie-file.ts","start_line":22,"end_line":61}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-fd1760898ac44fcba9f1897d5dccfd62","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-gemini-web/scripts/gemini-webapi/utils/cookie-file.ts","start_line":64,"end_line":78},"finding":null,"explanation":"This function persists a cookie map and optional source value to a filesystem path, which is a safety-relevant file write involving authentication/session data. The code contains no confirmation prompt, logging, comment, or docstring warning users that sensitive cookie material will be stored locally.","remediation":"Add a clear user-facing disclosure or documented warning that cookies will be written to a local file at the resolved path, and note that the file may contain sensitive session data. If appropriate, also add logging, comments, or a confirmation step before persisting credentials.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-gemini-web/scripts/gemini-webapi/utils/cookie-file.ts","start_line":64,"end_line":78}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-3abecfe312194aaa9cda27c65cdb51b7","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-gemini-web/scripts/gemini-webapi/utils/get-access-token.ts","start_line":40,"end_line":63},"finding":null,"explanation":"The helper scans a local data directory for cached Google session cookie components and reuses them for authentication. Reconstructing authentication from cached credential files is a stronger capability than ordinary web-to-markdown or web-fetch behavior and is not clearly justified by the stated scraping purpose.","remediation":"Avoid automatic discovery of cached credential files unless the manifest explicitly declares this behavior; prefer explicit user-provided credentials or a clearly documented login flow.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-gemini-web/scripts/gemini-webapi/utils/get-access-token.ts","start_line":40,"end_line":63}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-1d60fe6084654af0846a4f842c87394c","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.86,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-gemini-web/scripts/gemini-webapi/utils/get-access-token.ts","start_line":79,"end_line":189},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest positions this subskill as Gemini网页抓取, but this function's main responsibility is assembling cookies from multiple sources, probing Google endpoints, loading browser cookies, and caching authenticated session material. That is broader than straightforward web retrieval and reflects an authentication/session-management subsystem.","remediation":"Update the skill description to state that it authenticates against Gemini using browser/cached cookies, or narrow the code so the skill only performs fetching with explicitly supplied authentication.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-gemini-web/scripts/gemini-webapi/utils/get-access-token.ts","start_line":79,"end_line":189}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-8a5297e143964e06a1b3ac055e427038","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-gemini-web/scripts/gemini-webapi/utils/get-access-token.ts","start_line":94,"end_line":99},"finding":null,"explanation":"This skill is described as Gemini web scraping, but this helper goes beyond fetching web content and actively loads authenticated browser cookies from local browser state, then later persists them to disk for reuse. Accessing and reusing local login cookies is a sensitive capability that is not obviously justified by a generic '网页抓取' description alone.","remediation":"Explicitly document that the skill imports authenticated browser cookies and caches them locally, or constrain the implementation to only use user-supplied cookies/token material without inspecting browser state.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-gemini-web/scripts/gemini-webapi/utils/get-access-token.ts","start_line":94,"end_line":99}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-44f5d5a2798044f2870cbf684b2f325f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-gemini-web/scripts/gemini-webapi/utils/get-access-token.ts","start_line":96,"end_line":101},"finding":null,"explanation":"This code loads cookies from the user's browser via Chrome CDP and later persists cookies to disk, which are safety-sensitive credential-handling operations. In this file, those actions have no confirmation prompt and no clear user-facing disclosure beyond verbose debug logging, so users may not realize browser cookies are being accessed and reused.","remediation":"Add a clear user-facing warning or confirmation before loading b