clipboard during HTML/image insertion. Consider prompting the user before clipboard-modifying steps or preserving/restoring clipboard contents when feasible.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-wechat/scripts/wechat-article.ts","start_line":96,"end_line":97}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-b3af6c536a6a4c0092e3b1198eebefd6","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-wechat/scripts/wechat-article.ts","start_line":672,"end_line":673},"finding":null,"explanation":"This code performs a state-changing action on the user's WeChat account by clicking the save button and persisting the article as a draft. Although there is logging immediately before the click, the visible CLI help does not clearly warn that running the script will modify the account by saving content remotely, and there is no confirmation prompt before doing so.","remediation":"Add an explicit user-facing warning in the usage/help text and/or a confirmation prompt before saving the draft. If saving is always intended, document clearly that the script will create or update a draft in the connected WeChat account.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-wechat/scripts/wechat-article.ts","start_line":672,"end_line":673}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-8e4a3cd33d8c4898aaac8dfd695800a6","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-wechat/scripts/wechat-article.ts","start_line":707,"end_line":707},"finding":null,"explanation":"The usage text documents `--submit` as the control for saving a draft, implying draft-saving is conditional on that flag. In actual execution, `postArticle()` always clicks the save button at L672-L673 and never checks the `submit` option, so the documented intent contradicts the implemented behavior.","remediation":"Either honor the `submit` flag by gating the draft-save action on `submit === true`, or update the help text and option naming to reflect that drafting always occurs.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-wechat/scripts/wechat-article.ts","start_line":707,"end_line":707}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-bace985dfcf54f7583915570e3dfd93f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-wechat/scripts/wechat-extend-config.ts","start_line":199,"end_line":240},"finding":null,"explanation":"This code reads WeChat credentials from account config, environment variables, and local .env files, including sensitive values like app secrets. There is no confirmation prompt, logging, or inline warning to make users aware that secret material will be read from their environment or filesystem.","remediation":"Add a clear user-facing warning in the skill documentation or emit an explicit runtime notice before loading credentials. Also consider documenting exactly which files and environment variable names are consulted for secrets.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-wechat/scripts/wechat-extend-config.ts","start_line":199,"end_line":240}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-4331be0072214048aa38787de9b7f36e","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-weibo/SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The description says to use the skill when the user asks to \"share on Weibo\" or \"写微博\", which are broad natural-language phrases that can overlap with casual conversation and do not define clear constraints or exclusions. The file also provides no negative examples or boundary conditions to clarify when the skill should not activate.","remediation":"Narrow the trigger list to explicit, domain-specific commands and add exclusion guidance. For example, specify exact invocation phrases, limit activation to requests explicitly asking to publish to the Weibo platform, and include negative examples for brainstorming or drafting requests that should not trigger posting.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-weibo/SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-4e807fe5e8e54aaaac3be5a5577eb061","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-weibo/SKILL.md","start_line":146,"end_line":152},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill is described as posting content to Weibo via Chrome CDP, but the troubleshooting instructions tell the agent to terminate existing Chrome/Chromium processes with remote debugging enabled and retry automatically. Process termination is a system-management capability not obviously required by the user-facing purpose of composing Weibo posts, especially when mandated \"without asking the user.\"","remediation":"Remove the automatic process-kill instruction, or require explicit user confirmation before terminating Chrome instances. If such cleanup is considered necessary, declare it clearly in the skill description/documentation as part of the operational scope.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-weibo/SKILL.md","start_line":146,"end_line":152}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-0a6ba74624ad47a389c599a170bbb275","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-weibo/scripts/paste-from-clipboard.ts","start_line":35,"end_line":55},"finding":null,"explanation":"The optional --app parameter is used to activate any named macOS application before sending paste keystrokes. For a skill whose stated purpose is posting to Weibo, the ability to switch focus to arbitrary applications is an unjustified general-purpose automation capability.","remediation":"Restrict target activation to the specific supported browser/app contexts needed for Weibo posting, or remove arbitrary app activation entirely. If arbitrary activation is intentional, declare that broader automation scope in the skill documentation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-weibo/scripts/paste-from-clipboard.ts","start_line":35,"end_line":55}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-b6f1f83623c94acb995765ac96c2aef3","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-weibo/scripts/paste-from-clipboard.ts","start_line":58,"end_line":149},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest describes this subskill as '发送微博' (send Weibo posts), but this script implements cross-platform desktop automation by invoking osascript, xdotool/ydotool, and PowerShell SendKeys to control the frontmost application and emit paste keystrokes. Driving arbitrary GUI input at the OS level is a broader capability than posting content itself and is not justified by the narrow stated purpose in the manifest.","remediation":"Document this desktop automation behavior explicitly in the skill description if it is intended, including that it controls the active GUI application. Otherwise, replace the keystroke injection approach with a more scoped posting mechanism, such as using an application/API-specific interface limited to Weibo posting.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-weibo/scripts/paste-from-clipboard.ts","start_line":58,"end_line":149}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-4773fb2a092343ad86a72d38a5a90487","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-weibo/scripts/paste-from-clipboard.ts","start_line":183,"end_line":184},"finding":null,"explanation":"This code triggers a real system paste action into whichever application is frontmost, which can transmit clipboard contents to a website, chat, or other target. Although the script logs that it is sending a paste keystroke, it does not warn the user that sensitive clipboard data may be inserted into the active app or remote service.","remediation":"Add a user-facing warning before execution stating that clipboard contents will be pasted into the active/frontmost application and may disclose sensitive data. Consider requiring explicit confirmation unless the caller has already specified the target context.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-weibo/scripts/paste-from-clipboard.ts","start_line":183,"end_line":184}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-0f67df4b66b044b08fbe776f6b659d0e","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.79,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-weibo/scripts/vendor/baoyu-chrome-cdp/src/index.ts","start_line":200,"end_line":317},"finding":null,"explanation":"The functions parse DevToolsActivePort files, inspect Chrome user data directories, and enumerate local processes to locate running debug-enabled Chrome instances. This accesses local application state that may be privacy-sensitive, but the code contains no user-facing warning, logging, or explanatory docstring/comment disclosing that behavior.","remediation":"Add clear disclosure in code comments/docstrings and skill documentation that the skill inspects local Chrome profile directories and running processes to discover an existing debugging session, and log or otherwise surface that action when it occurs.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-weibo/scripts/vendor/baoyu-chrome-cdp/src/index.ts","start_line":200,"end_line":317}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-8a43202ab87f43038b091068756f61ac","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-weibo/scripts/vendor/baoyu-chrome-cdp/src/index.ts","start_line":211,"end_line":317},"finding":null,"explanation":"This file, embedded under the Weibo posting skill, does more than open or automate a browser for posting: it scans local Chrome profile directories, reads DevToolsActivePort files, inspects running processes via `ps`, and attaches to any matching existing Chrome remote-debugging session. Those capabilities enable discovery and takeover of pre-existing browser sessions, which is not obviously required by the stated purpose of \"发送微博\" and materially expands what the skill can interact with.","remediation":"Limit the helper to launching and controlling only a dedicated Chrome instance/profile created for this skill. Remove reuse/discovery of existing Chrome sessions and process scanning unless the manifest explicitly states this browser-session attachment behavior.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-weibo/scripts/vendor/baoyu-chrome-cdp/src/index.ts","start_line":211,"end_line":317}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-64dbbe04ebcd4c0f868a96ef9922c74b","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.81,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-weibo/scripts/vendor/baoyu-chrome-cdp/src/index.ts","start_line":460,"end_line":474},"finding":null,"explanation":"The `launchChrome` helper starts a local browser process and accepts unrestricted `extraArgs`, allowing callers to enable additional Chrome features or debugging behaviors beyond straightforward Weibo posting automation. For a skill whose stated purpose is simply sending Weibo posts, exposing generic browser-launch customization is broader than the declared intent.","remediation":"Constrain browser launch to a fixed, minimal argument set needed for posting. If extra launch flexibility is required, document it explicitly in the skill description and restrict accepted arguments through an allowlist.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-weibo/scripts/vendor/baoyu-chrome-cdp/src/index.ts","start_line":460,"end_line":474}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-73a739861b4f4ceea8dcf10f9ea7b360","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-weibo/scripts/vendor/baoyu-chrome-cdp/src/index.ts","start_line":460,"end_line":486},"finding":null,"explanation":"This file launches a browser subprocess with a persistent user-data directory and later force-kills it, which is a safety-relevant system operation. There is no confirmation prompt, logging, print statement, or explanatory comment near the launch/kill functions to disclose this behavior to a user.","remediation":"Add a clear user-facing disclosure or confirmation before launching and terminating Chrome, or include explicit comments/docstrings and ensure the skill documentation warns that it starts and may forcibly stop a local Chrome process using the specified profile directory.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-weibo/scripts/vendor/baoyu-chrome-cdp/src/index.ts","start_line":460,"end_line":486}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-d09d34e4c43c4fb7acfcfd5d88264a1f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-weibo/scripts/vendor/baoyu-md/src/extensions/plantuml.ts","start_line":142,"end_line":145},"finding":null,"explanation":"This code constructs a URL to the public PlantUML server that embeds the user-provided diagram source in encoded form, causing diagram contents to be transmitted off-system when the rendered image is loaded. Although comments describe the server URL, there is no explicit user-facing warning, confirmation, or disclosure near the network behavior itself.","remediation":"Add a clear warning in code comments and the skill documentation that PlantUML content will be sent to the configured server for rendering. Consider requiring explicit opt-in for non-local servers, or defaulting to a self-hosted/local renderer when privacy matters.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-weibo/scripts/vendor/baoyu-md/src/extensions/plantuml.ts","start_line":142,"end_line":145}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-1695a3cb62514b00ba52f376abab5fc2","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-weibo/scripts/vendor/baoyu-md/src/extensions/plantuml.ts","start_line":167,"end_line":167},"finding":null,"explanation":"When inlineSvg is enabled, the code performs a fetch to retrieve SVG content from the PlantUML server. The operation is safety-relevant because it transmits rendered-diagram request data to a remote endpoint, but the code only logs failures and does not provide a user-facing warning or confirmation about this network access.","remediation":"Document and surface that enabling inlineSvg performs remote fetches to the configured PlantUML server. Add a visible notice, configuration flag description, or explicit opt-in before making external requests.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-weibo/scripts/vendor/baoyu-md/src/extensions/plantuml.ts","start_line":167,"end_line":167}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-d8cf558fa17d4c6aaf4db2ca442ae27d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-weibo/scripts/vendor/baoyu-md/src/extensions/slider.ts","start_line":51,"end_line":66},"finding":null,"explanation":"The generated HTML forces a Chinese font family (`微软雅黑`) and displays the instruction text `<<< 左右滑动看更多 >>>`, which imposes a specific language/locale on all users. This is a natural-language policy issue because the skill does not offer user opt-in or document that the extension is intentionally limited to a Chinese-only context.","remediation":"Make the instructional text and font configurable based on user or environment locale, or document clearly that this renderer is only for a Chinese/WeChat-specific audience. If the locale is intentional, add explicit justification in comments or surrounding documentation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-weibo/scripts/vendor/baoyu-md/src/extensions/slider.ts","start_line":51,"end_line":66}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-559eb715bc094eb6aca1261769152856","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"packages/baoyu-md/src/cli.ts","start_line":15,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"npx commands without a version suffix (e.g. @1.0.0) create a rug-pull risk if the upstream server is compromised and publishes a malicious update.","remediation":"Pin the version: npx @scope/server@1.2.3","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"c4192318b5e992b01b5d662b1759272d7e627eb792d40d90d04ed8bba9b08121","occurrences":[{"file":"packages/baoyu-md/src/cli.ts","start_line":15,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-559eb715bc094eb6aca1261769152856","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"packages/baoyu-md/src/render.ts","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"npx commands wit