ation":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-weibo/scripts/weibo-article.ts","start_line":122,"end_line":157},"finding":null,"explanation":"The automation explicitly searches for Chinese UI text such as \"写文章\", \"请输入标题\", and related selectors, which means the skill only works against a specific language/localized interface. Because the file does not offer a user language choice or clearly document this as a justified locale-specific constraint within the code, it is a natural-language locale policy concern.","remediation":"Document the Chinese-locale requirement clearly and justify it as a Weibo-specific regional constraint, or add configuration to support multiple UI languages/locales and let the user opt in to the expected locale.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-weibo/scripts/weibo-article.ts","start_line":122,"end_line":157}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-9ceefb1c535547288927afd7ee4f4829","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-x/SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The description says to use the skill when the user asks to \"post to X\", \"tweet\", \"publish to Twitter\", or \"share on X\". Terms like \"tweet\" and \"share on X\" are relatively broad in everyday conversation, and the file does not provide exclusion conditions or negative examples to clarify when the skill should not activate.","remediation":"Narrow the trigger language to explicit, task-oriented phrases and add scope constraints or negative examples. For example, specify that the skill should activate only when the user explicitly wants to compose or publish content to their own X account via browser automation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-x/SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-b5a29a4a72814b08acc9e055ff178ff7","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-x/SKILL.md","start_line":207,"end_line":213},"finding":null,"explanation":"The stated purpose is to help post content to X via a browser workflow. However, the troubleshooting instructions explicitly tell the agent to run `pkill` against Chrome/Chromium CDP instances and even do so automatically without asking the user, which is host-level process management unrelated to the core semantic purpose of composing a post.","remediation":"Remove automatic process-killing instructions from the skill, or require explicit user confirmation before terminating browser processes. If such recovery behavior is truly intended, declare it clearly as part of the skill's operational scope.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-x/SKILL.md","start_line":207,"end_line":213}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-322ca73eeff34905ac48c50f687b35c3","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-x/SKILL.md","start_line":213,"end_line":213},"finding":null,"explanation":"The markdown instructs the agent to automatically kill existing Chrome CDP instances and retry without asking the user. Terminating browser processes can disrupt active sessions or unsaved work, but this section does not include a clear user-facing warning about that impact before performing the action.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning that killing Chrome/Chromium CDP instances may close active automated browser sessions or interrupt work, and instruct the agent to notify the user before doing so unless they have already opted in.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-x/SKILL.md","start_line":213,"end_line":213}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-46c40289fa38417fa344acb37bcd48f0","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-x/references/regular-posts.md","start_line":54,"end_line":54},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file explains that images are copied to the system clipboard and later pasted by keyboard shortcut, which can affect user data in the clipboard and interact with the active system UI. While the mechanics are documented, there is no clear cautionary warning to users that existing clipboard contents may be overwritten and that the automation will control the frontmost application.","remediation":"Add a prominent warning near the workflow and image support sections stating that the skill overwrites the system clipboard, brings Chrome/frontmost apps to focus, and sends paste keystrokes to the OS; advise users to save clipboard contents and ensure the correct window is focused before running.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-x/references/regular-posts.md","start_line":54,"end_line":54}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-2966a8f5b2c841a7a0a9ef939477e91e","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.79,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-x/references/regular-posts.md","start_line":73,"end_line":73},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file states that users log in manually and that cookies are saved, and later documents use of a persistent profile directory for saved login sessions. Because this behavior stores authentication state and browser data, the skill description should explicitly warn users about persistence of account/session data on disk.","remediation":"Add a user-facing warning that the skill stores browser profile data and login sessions persistently, including where the profile is stored, how to clear it, and the privacy/security implications of reusing saved cookies.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-x/references/regular-posts.md","start_line":73,"end_line":73}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-4a8e74693641436bb262ae6a37b1cc58","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-x/references/regular-posts.md","start_line":83,"end_line":89},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill is described as '发送X帖子' (posting to X), but this documentation explicitly instructs using Chrome DevTools Protocol with '--disable-blink-features=AutomationControlled' and describes bypassing X's anti-automation detection. Evasion of platform automation defenses is not an obvious or necessary part of the stated posting purpose and represents an additional capability with higher-risk intent.","remediation":"Remove or avoid guidance focused on evading platform automation detection. Document only legitimate posting mechanisms necessary for composing or submitting posts, and if browser automation is required, describe it without stealth or bypass techniques.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-x/references/regular-posts.md","start_line":83,"end_line":89}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-6696a688e2e34ebcae2c24c3b4cf94f0","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.81,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-x/references/regular-posts.md","start_line":83,"end_line":100},"finding":null,"explanation":"This section describes launching Chrome with automation-evasion settings, bringing Chrome to the foreground, and sending real Cmd+V keystrokes through osascript/System Events. These behaviors can affect the local system and active applications, but the document frames them as implementation details rather than clearly warning users about the operational and safety implications.","remediation":"Add a prominent warning in the 'How It Works' or earlier usage section that the skill performs OS-level UI automation, may manipulate the focused application, requires elevated accessibility permissions, and should only be run when the user is ready and the target window is confirmed.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-x/references/regular-posts.md","start_line":83,"end_line":100}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-99edcfbfc27c406e96775833ac6ba301","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-x/scripts/md-to-html.ts","start_line":108,"end_line":176},"finding":null,"explanation":"Although this file is named and documented as converting Markdown to HTML, it also fetches remote HTTPS images referenced in the Markdown or cover metadata and stores them locally. That goes beyond pure format conversion and adds network retrieval side effects that are not implied by a straightforward Markdown-to-HTML transformation.","remediation":"Update the skill/documentation to explicitly state that remote images are downloaded and cached locally during conversion, or remove network fetching from this helper and require callers to provide local image assets separately.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-x/scripts/md-to-html.ts","start_line":108,"end_line":176}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-73aa9746bf994e0ca51e314f955ca539","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-x/scripts/md-to-html.ts","start_line":163,"end_line":185},"finding":null,"explanation":"For a converter utility, resolving image paths to remote URLs and downloading them is a broader capability than necessary to transform Markdown syntax into HTML. This introduces network access and local caching behavior that is not an obvious requirement of conversion itself.","remediation":"Restrict image handling to local path resolution only, or make remote fetching an explicit opt-in option clearly declared as part of the skill's scope.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-x/scripts/md-to-html.ts","start_line":163,"end_line":185}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-d287e71e14c849dbbc5bf0dc2552c9b2","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.86,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-x/scripts/md-to-html.ts","start_line":168,"end_line":176},"finding":null,"explanation":"When markdown contains HTTPS image URLs, the script automatically makes outbound network requests to fetch them. Although there is a console message at download time, the CLI usage text does not warn users that processing a markdown file may contact external hosts based on document contents, which is a relevant privacy and safety disclosure for a conversion utility.","remediation":"Add an explicit user-facing warning in the usage/help text and/or module comments that remote images will be downloaded when HTTPS URLs are present. Consider adding a flag to disable network fetching or require opt-in for remote downloads.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-x/scripts/md-to-html.ts","start_line":168,"end_line":176}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-e5f090f3e3af4ae2a4b6506b9a73720c","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.82,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-x/scripts/paste-from-clipboard.ts","start_line":5,"end_line":7},"finding":null,"explanation":"The usage text describes bypassing CDP synthetic events that websites can detect, implying a website-scoped workaround. In reality, the implementation sends real system keystrokes to whichever application is frontmost or activates a named app first, which is a broader OS-level action than the documentation suggests.","remediation":"Revise the help/documentation to state explicitly that the script performs system-wide UI automation by invoking platform tools to send paste keystrokes to the frontmost or specified application.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-x/scripts/paste-from-clipboard.ts","start_line":5,"end_line":7}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-b87e1f5e9d694705b5c26c597c72f050","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"CHANGELOG.md","start_line":336,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"npx commands without a version suffix (e.g. @1.0.0) create a rug-pull risk if the upstream server is compromised and publishes a malicious update.","remediation":"Pin the version: npx @scope/server@1.2.3","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"1e9f7de7dbda51be7189ae52a5639afaa7a0fa22862ffa08b60755cb17de8c08","occurrences":[{"file":"CHANGELOG.md","start_line":336,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-b87e1f5e9d694705b5c26c597c72f050","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"CHANGELOG.zh.md","start_line":336,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"npx commands without a version suffix (e.g. @1.0.0) create a rug-pull risk if the upstream server is compromised and publishes a malicious update.","remediation":"Pin the version: npx @scope/server@1.2.3","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"1e9f7de7dbda51be7189ae52a5639afaa7a0fa22862ffa08b60755cb17de8c08","occurrences":[{"file":"CHANGELOG.zh.md","start_line":336,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-b87e1f5e9d694705b5c26c597c72f050","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confide