,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"npx commands without a version suffix (e.g. @1.0.0) create a rug-pull risk if the upstream server is compromised and publishes a malicious update.","remediation":"Pin the version: npx @scope/server@1.2.3","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"1e9f7de7dbda51be7189ae52a5639afaa7a0fa22862ffa08b60755cb17de8c08","occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-slide-deck/SKILL.md","start_line":35,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-b87e1f5e9d694705b5c26c597c72f050","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-translate/SKILL.md","start_line":20,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"npx commands without a version suffix (e.g. @1.0.0) create a rug-pull risk if the upstream server is compromised and publishes a malicious update.","remediation":"Pin the version: npx @scope/server@1.2.3","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"1e9f7de7dbda51be7189ae52a5639afaa7a0fa22862ffa08b60755cb17de8c08","occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-translate/SKILL.md","start_line":20,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-b87e1f5e9d694705b5c26c597c72f050","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-translate/scripts/main.ts","start_line":19,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"npx commands without a version suffix (e.g. @1.0.0) create a rug-pull risk if the upstream server is compromised and publishes a malicious update.","remediation":"Pin the version: npx @scope/server@1.2.3","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"1e9f7de7dbda51be7189ae52a5639afaa7a0fa22862ffa08b60755cb17de8c08","occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-translate/scripts/main.ts","start_line":19,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-b87e1f5e9d694705b5c26c597c72f050","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-url-to-markdown/SKILL.md","start_line":25,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"npx commands without a version suffix (e.g. @1.0.0) create a rug-pull risk if the upstream server is compromised and publishes a malicious update.","remediation":"Pin the version: npx @scope/server@1.2.3","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"1e9f7de7dbda51be7189ae52a5639afaa7a0fa22862ffa08b60755cb17de8c08","occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-url-to-markdown/SKILL.md","start_line":25,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-91552eb392f346e781d1491585619998","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-x/scripts/paste-from-clipboard.ts","start_line":58,"end_line":149},"finding":null,"explanation":"This file does not just format or submit content to X; it programmatically drives the operating system to send real paste keystrokes using osascript, xdotool/ydotool, and PowerShell SendKeys. For a skill whose stated purpose is '发送X帖子', OS-level input injection is a materially broader capability that is not independently justified by the manifest text.","remediation":"Document this UI-automation capability explicitly in the skill manifest or narrow the implementation to a direct X-posting/API/browser automation path that does not synthesize global OS input. If retained, constrain the helper to a declared target context and add clear permission/usage documentation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-x/scripts/paste-from-clipboard.ts","start_line":58,"end_line":149}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-08bf758b5e2e4d32adaac2ba249b6f67","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-x/scripts/x-article.ts","start_line":695,"end_line":709},"finding":null,"explanation":"This code performs an irreversible external action by clicking the publish button and logging success, but it does not ask the user for runtime confirmation before posting. While the usage text mentions that --submit will publish, the execution path itself lacks any confirmation safeguard for this safety-critical action.","remediation":"Add an interactive confirmation prompt before clicking Publish when submit is true, or require an explicit second confirmation flag such as --yes. Also emit a clear pre-publication warning immediately before the publish action describing that the article will be posted to the user's X account.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-x/scripts/x-article.ts","start_line":695,"end_line":709}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-dc845f3bb0324e3892f11257612f176f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-x/scripts/x-quote.ts","start_line":32,"end_line":183},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest lists this subskill as '发送X帖子', which suggests composing and sending a normal X post. This file specifically automates opening an existing tweet, invoking the retweet menu, selecting the quote option, optionally adding commentary, and submitting a quote post, which is a more specific behavior than the stated description.","remediation":"Clarify the manifest/skill documentation to explicitly include quote-posting/reposting capabilities, or separate this logic into a distinctly named subskill for quoting existing tweets.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-post-to-x/scripts/x-quote.ts","start_line":32,"end_line":183}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-dfbcd2687ab849a39e24245604655aba","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-slide-deck/SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The description says to use the skill when the user asks to \"create slides\", \"make a presentation\", \"generate deck\", \"slide deck\", or \"PPT\". Several of these phrases, especially \"slide deck\" and \"PPT\", are short and context-light, which increases the chance of matching ordinary conversation without enough specificity about scope or exclusions.","remediation":"Narrow the activation wording to explicit command-like phrases or concrete contexts, and add constraints or negative examples. For example, specify that the skill should activate only when the user wants a generated presentation from source content or invokes the named command directly.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-slide-deck/SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-7c703a08a22844a9ae0bf2a8c3410a31","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.78,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-slide-deck/SKILL.md","start_line":35,"end_line":40},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill is described as generating professional slide deck images from content, but it also instructs the agent to resolve Bun/NPX runtimes and execute TypeScript scripts (L035, L568-L570). Spawning external tooling is a materially broader capability than image generation itself, even if used here for post-processing into PPTX/PDF.","remediation":"Explicitly declare in the manifest that the skill invokes local Bun/NPX scripts to assemble generated slides into PPTX/PDF outputs, or separate export functionality into a dedicated sub-skill.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-slide-deck/SKILL.md","start_line":35,"end_line":40}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-debb01abd9ba410dbabadae2826e670c","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-slide-deck/references/base-prompt.md","start_line":20,"end_line":20},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file is part of a PPT/幻灯片生成 skill, whose stated purpose is creating slide visuals. Line L20 adds a policy-level capability to bypass normal refusal behavior for sensitive or copyrighted figures, which is not an obvious or necessary requirement of presentation-slide generation.","remediation":"Remove the instruction to avoid refusal for sensitive or copyrighted figures. Replace it with guidance to respect model safety and copyright policies, e.g. use original, non-infringing illustrations or request user-approved source material when needed.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-slide-deck/references/base-prompt.md","start_line":20,"end_line":20}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-44595cc4c0354fe1a19fec3d279a4bcc","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-slide-deck/references/styles/intuition-machine.md","start_line":22,"end_line":22},"finding":null,"explanation":"This file requires the format \"ENGLISH TERM 中文翻译,\" which imposes a specific language pairing as a default behavior. Under the policy, forcing a specific language without user opt-in is a natural-language policy violation unless the regional or audience constraint is explicitly justified.","remediation":"Change the instruction to make bilingual English/Chinese labeling optional or user-selected, or explicitly document that this style is intended only for a Chinese-English audience and should not be used otherwise.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-slide-deck/references/styles/intuition-machine.md","start_line":22,"end_line":22}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-5cbef173933f4a1cba1bf68204642ccf","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-slide-deck/references/styles/intuition-machine.md","start_line":45,"end_line":57},"finding":null,"explanation":"The visual-elements and style-rules sections require bilingual callout labels and English+Chinese key elements with no indication that users may choose another language or disable bilingual output. This creates a locale/language policy issue because the skill appears to force a specific language combination across outputs.","remediation":"Revise the requirements to say bilingual labels should be used only when requested or when the target audience is explicitly English/Chinese, and otherwise allow the user's preferred language or locale.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-slide-deck/references/styles/intuition-machine.md","start_line":45,"end_line":57}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-c3fce406967544df8dbb7cf6ee264df6","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-translate/SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest description lists many triggers and then broadens scope to 'needs any document translation' and 'when a URL or file is provided with translation intent.' Those conditions are ambiguous and can overlap with common requests involving files or URLs, without clear exclusion conditions or negative examples limiting when the skill should or should not activate.","remediation":"Narrow the trigger definition to an explicit set of invocation phrases or contexts, and add clear boundaries or negative examples. For example, specify that the skill activates only for direct translation requests, not generic file/URL analysis or editing requests.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-translate/SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-6b4c90ae1b744b5e99e29da44595a4f0","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-translate/SKILL.md","start_line":74,"end_line":74},"finding":null,"explanation":"The defaults section sets the target language to 'zh-CN', which imposes a specific locale/language behavior unless overridden. This is a natural-language policy concern because the skill does not present language choice as opt-in at the point of default behavior.","remediation":"Make the target language unset by default and require explicit user selection, or clearly ask the user to choose a target language before first translation. Alternatively, document a justified region-specific scope for the skill if Chinese-default behavior is intentional.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-translate/SKILL.md","start_line":74,"end_line":74}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-3997ce8aa2794829ba3aa59cf86d1abe","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-translate/references/subagent-prompt-template.md","start_line":40,"end_line":40},"finding":null,"explanation":"Line L40 hard-codes translator's notes in Chinese format using Chinese text and punctuation: `译文（English original，通俗解释）`. This imposes a specific language/locale convention in a reusable translation template without offering user choice or explaining that the skill is limited to Chinese-target translations.","remediation":"Make the note format locale-neutral or parameterized by target language, e.g. `{translated term} ({original term}, {brief explanation in target language})`. If the skill is intentionally only for Chinese translations, document that scope explicitly in the skill description or template.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-translate/references/subagent-prompt-template.md","start_line":40,"end_line":40}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-bee1fac4380b4a7abbf1a075922ff327","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-translate/references/workflow-mechanics.md","start_line":10,"end_line":17},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file instructs the skill to save inline text to disk, fetch remote URL content, and create output directories, all of which can affect user data or system state. The description presents these actions as mechanics but does not include any warning about network access or filesystem modifications.","remediation":"Add a brief warning in the markdown that the workflow may fetch remote content and create or rename directories/files on the user's filesystem. Clarify when these actions occur and recommend user confirmation or review before execution.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-translate/references/workflow-mechanics.md","start_line":10,"end_line":17}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-ee0b78fa2b65427f8b0f8c4ba0bd3149","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-translate/references/workflow-mechanics.md","start_line":23,"end_line":25},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file specifies automatic renaming of an existing output directory to a timestamped backup path, which changes existing user files and directory names. Although it avoids overwriting, the markdown does not warn users that prior outputs will be renamed as part of the workflow.","remediation":"Document this behavior explicitly as a warning, noting that existing output directories will be renamed to backup directories before new results are created. Consider advising users to review or confirm this step when prior outputs are present.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-translate/references/workflow-mechanics.md","start_line":23,"end_line":25}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-13d2d0c2565d448b81e8ea351095c82a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-url-to-markdown/SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The description says \"Fetch any URL\" and \"Use when user wants to save a webpage as markdown,\" which defines invocation scope very broadly without explicit constraints or negative examples. In a manifest-style skill description, this can overlap with many ordinary browsing or note-taking requests and makes it unclear when this skill should or should not activate.","remediation":"Narrow the trigger description to specific intents and contexts, such as explicit requests to convert a webpage URL into markdown for local saving. Add exclusion examples or negative cases, e.g. not for general web browsing, summarization without saving, or non-URL content.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-url-to-markdown/SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-0062020ce3414e9fa07312f14b90b3ae","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-url-to-markdown/SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file states that the skill supports pages requiring login and can handle authenticated pages, but it does not explicitly warn users that captured output may include private account content from their active browser session. Because the tool saves both markdown and an HTML snapshot, this has privacy implications that should be disclosed in the markdown description.","remediation":"Add a prominent warning near the description or capture-mode section that using wait mode or authenticated capture can save private, account-specific page content to local files. Instruct users to verify they intend to capture logged-in content before proceeding.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-url-to-markdown/SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-299e7b867e2745a48caa53e682e80e41","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-x-to-markdown/SKILL.md","start_line":118,"end_line":null},"finding":"without asking","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"\n### First-Time Setup (BLOCKING)\n\n**CRITICAL**: When EXTEND.md is not found, you **MUST use `AskUserQuestion`** to ask the user for their preferences before creating EXTEND.md. **NEVER** create EXTEND.md with defaults without asking. This is a **BLOCKING** operation — do NOT proceed with any conversion until setup is complete.\n\nUse `AskUserQuestion` with ALL questions in ONE call:\n","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"8dc77d3dce9ba1f2672e813265a1b1a0c8594866ef38a4e978bf4f4451795465","occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-x-to-markdown/SKILL.md","start_line":118,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-299e7b867e2745a48caa53e682e80e41","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-format-markdown/SKILL.md","st