ntain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"\n### First-Time Setup (BLOCKING)\n\n**CRITICAL**: When EXTEND.md is not found, you **MUST use `AskUserQuestion`** to ask the user for their preferences before creating EXTEND.md. **NEVER** create EXTEND.md with defaults without asking. This is a **BLOCKING** operation — do NOT proceed with any conversion until setup is complete.\n\nUse `AskUserQuestion` with ALL questions in ONE call:\n","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"53c50b5f9db46aef2c9256d7fcc1d810ffe41283c629d53a831595fb8d19944c","occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-danger-x-to-markdown/SKILL.md","start_line":118,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-509ed0f9599f4be7bb309768d4259d94","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-url-to-markdown/SKILL.md","start_line":76,"end_line":null},"finding":"create EXTEND.md with defaults without asking. This is a **BLOCKING** operation — do NOT proceed with any conversion until setup is complete.\n\nUse `AskUserQuestion` with ALL questions in ONE call:\n\n**","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"\n### First-Time Setup (BLOCKING)\n\n**CRITICAL**: When EXTEND.md is not found, you **MUST use `AskUserQuestion`** to ask the user for their preferences before creating EXTEND.md. **NEVER** create EXTEND.md with defaults without asking. This is a **BLOCKING** operation — do NOT proceed with any conversion until setup is complete.\n\nUse `AskUserQuestion` with ALL questions in ONE call:\n","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"53c50b5f9db46aef2c9256d7fcc1d810ffe41283c629d53a831595fb8d19944c","occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-url-to-markdown/SKILL.md","start_line":76,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-5859c23c84c441b28b4ed9f28bb53e66","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-url-to-markdown/SKILL.md","start_line":124,"end_line":124},"finding":null,"explanation":"The markdown notes that local capture can fall back to the hosted defuddle.md API, and later names the endpoint, but it does not clearly present this as a user-facing privacy warning. Sending a requested URL to an external service can expose browsing targets or sensitive internal links, so the description should explicitly disclose that network transmission occurs.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning in the feature list or Hosted API Fallback section stating that fallback sends the URL, and potentially page-derived processing context, to an external service. Recommend disabling or avoiding fallback for sensitive, private, internal, or authenticated pages.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-url-to-markdown/SKILL.md","start_line":124,"end_line":124}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-6350a589b7104939bf86e4b9e5acee77","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-url-to-markdown/scripts/main.ts","start_line":100,"end_line":106},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill is described as converting a URL to Markdown, but the code includes a fallback that calls defuddle.md with the user-supplied URL when local capture fails. While network access to fetch the page is expected, outsourcing conversion to an external service is a materially different behavior that the manifest description does not disclose.","remediation":"Document that failed captures may be retried via the external defuddle.md service, including any data-sharing implications, or remove the remote fallback if the skill should remain purely local.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-url-to-markdown/scripts/main.ts","start_line":100,"end_line":106}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-cd91b9a3e88a498ca77ff9469870a98f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-url-to-markdown/scripts/main.ts","start_line":254,"end_line":256},"finding":null,"explanation":"The stated subskill purpose is 'URL转Markdown', which implies converting a URL's content into Markdown output. This implementation additionally derives a second output path and writes the captured raw HTML of the page to disk, creating an artifact beyond the described Markdown conversion behavior.","remediation":"Either update the skill description/documentation to explicitly state that it stores an HTML snapshot alongside the Markdown, or remove/make optional the HTML snapshot persistence so behavior matches the declared URL-to-Markdown scope.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-url-to-markdown/scripts/main.ts","start_line":254,"end_line":256}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-a2e8032184c84a95a25b94f6d5f1d51f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-url-to-markdown/scripts/markdown-conversion-shared.ts","start_line":212,"end_line":305},"finding":null,"explanation":"This code extracts metadata and body content from arbitrary HTML and then assembles it into a Markdown document, including fields such as URL, author, published date, language, and raw converted content. That is a file-generation/data-transformation operation on untrusted external content, but the file contains no confirmation prompt, logging, or explanatory comment/docstring warning that fetched page content and metadata will be written into output artifacts.","remediation":"Add a visible disclosure in code comments/docstrings or user-facing logging that the skill captures page HTML/metadata and writes them into generated Markdown/YAML output. If this is invoked interactively, consider a confirmation step before persisting converted content.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-url-to-markdown/scripts/markdown-conversion-shared.ts","start_line":212,"end_line":305}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-ecf144ccd789409490a1ee9c267f1ba5","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.86,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-url-to-markdown/scripts/media-localizer.ts","start_line":247,"end_line":278},"finding":null,"explanation":"This function performs two safety-relevant actions: it fetches remote URLs and writes the downloaded content into local imgs/videos directories. While failures are logged, there is no user-facing disclosure or confirmation that remote content will be retrieved and saved locally, which can affect privacy, bandwidth, and local filesystem state.","remediation":"Add a clear user-facing warning or confirmation before downloading and saving remote media, or document this behavior prominently in the skill's markdown/README. At minimum, emit an explicit log/message before the operation stating that remote media will be fetched and stored under the markdown file's directory.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-url-to-markdown/scripts/media-localizer.ts","start_line":247,"end_line":278}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-6d673f8899f8453f9bf6a16ec3a766e9","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-url-to-markdown/scripts/vendor/baoyu-chrome-cdp/src/index.ts","start_line":211,"end_line":317},"finding":null,"explanation":"This file belongs to the URL-to-Markdown skill, whose stated purpose is converting a URL into Markdown. While launching a browser for rendering can be justified, this code goes further by scanning default Chrome user-data directories, reading DevToolsActivePort files, and parsing `ps aux` output to discover and attach to already-running Chrome instances. That capability reaches into unrelated local browser state and is not obviously required by the skill's declared purpose.","remediation":"Avoid attaching to arbitrary existing Chrome sessions. Prefer launching an isolated Chrome instance with a dedicated temporary profile for the conversion task, or require explicit opt-in before reusing a pre-existing browser/debug session.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-url-to-markdown/scripts/vendor/baoyu-chrome-cdp/src/index.ts","start_line":211,"end_line":317}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-6ddcc2bad6a747f58e940fcfe4a2bde1","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-xhs-images/references/config/first-time-setup.md","start_line":33,"end_line":null},"finding":"Create EXTEND.md    │\n└─────────────────────┘\n        │\n        ▼\n    Continue to Step 1\n```\n\n## Questions\n\n**Language**: Use user's input language or saved language preference.\n\nUse single AskUserQue","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"        │\n        ▼\n┌─────────────────────┐\n│ Create EXTEND.md    │\n└─────────────────────┘\n        │\n        ▼","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"3bb9a85c2ff4c0fbd4e3854a1789b7990a8222d1d7ae103877c48f1c50e22459","occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-xhs-images/references/config/first-time-setup.md","start_line":33,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-553edd0fc9454c6fbaa964d27e7977dc","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.81,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-xhs-images/references/workflows/analysis-framework.md","start_line":129,"end_line":130},"finding":null,"explanation":"The sample output hard-codes both `source_language: zh` and `user_language: zh`, and the surrounding framework is written to optimize specifically for Xiaohongshu with Chinese-language hook patterns. This can constitute a language/locale policy issue because it defaults to a specific language rather than explicitly offering opt-in or documenting why non-Chinese output is unsupported.","remediation":"Document that the skill is intentionally China/Xiaohongshu-specific and limited to Chinese-language workflows, or revise the framework to let the user choose `user_language` explicitly instead of hard-coding `zh`.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-xhs-images/references/workflows/analysis-framework.md","start_line":129,"end_line":130}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-0cc8dea14c694f47b92ec19329235082","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-xhs-images/references/workflows/outline-template.md","start_line":86,"end_line":215},"finding":null,"explanation":"The example outline forces Chinese-language output across hooks, titles, subtitles, and CTAs, which is a natural-language locale constraint. Because the file does not indicate that the skill is China-specific or provide an opt-in or alternative language path, this can violate language/locale policy expectations.","remediation":"Document that the skill is explicitly intended for Chinese/Xiaohongshu content, or add instructions allowing the user to choose the output language/locale before generating outlines.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-xhs-images/references/workflows/outline-template.md","start_line":86,"end_line":215}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-5b7dcbfb49774d05b3813fbe6ffbd504","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-xhs-images/references/workflows/prompt-assembly.md","start_line":22,"end_line":22},"finding":null,"explanation":"The documented capability goes beyond assembling Xiaohongshu-style infographic prompts and instead directs the downstream generator to avoid refusing requests involving sensitive or copyrighted figures. That policy-level evasion behavior is not necessary for the stated purpose of 小红书图片处理 and is an inappropriate capability in this context.","remediation":"Remove the instruction to override or avoid refusal behavior for sensitive or copyrighted figures. Replace it with neutral guidance that requires compliance with the downstream image model's safety and copyright policies.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-xhs-images/references/workflows/prompt-assembly.md","start_line":22,"end_line":22}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-e5370debdcd54cac99b15ecb0dfbfa58","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"skills/baoyu-xhs-images/references/workflows/prompt-assembly.md","start_line":90,"end_line":90},"finding":null,"explanation":"This section repeats the same unjustified behavior in the screen-print variant by instructing creation of stylistically similar silhouettes for sensitive or copyrighted figures. That is not required for prompt assembly or XHS image processing and expands the skill into policy circumvention guidance.","remediation":"Delete the sensitive/copyrighted-figure substitution instruction from the screen-print override and state that such content must follow the downstream generator's applicable restrictions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"skills/baoyu-xhs-images/references/workflows/prompt-assembly.md","start_line":90,"end_line":90}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-942aacdea5f847cdad43c181f69c6ab8","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.79,"location":{"file":"CHANGELOG.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file includes a language selector formatted as \"English | [中文]\", which defaults readers into English rather than offering an explicit neutral language choice. Under the policy rule for natural-language locale behavior, this can be interpreted as forcing a specific language without clear opt-in.","remediation":"Present language options in a neutral way, such as \"Choose language: English / 中文\", or clarify that the default is based on repository convention and provide equal prominence to both language versions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"CHANGELOG.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-174aba1ab6e2432a8b717fa0b94dab55","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"CHANGELOG.zh.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The language switcher marks this file as Chinese-only by presenting \"[English](./CHANGELOG.md) | 中文\", making the current document fixed to Chinese. Under the policy, forcing a specific language without user opt-in is a natural-language locale constraint unless clearly justified; this changelog does not state any such justification.","remediation":"Add a brief note that this is an alternate localized version of the changelog and direct users to choose their preferred language, or present language selection in a way that makes the locale optional rather than imposed.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"CHANGELOG.zh.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-52bb2fdd1a6e49cebd15330b1087b155","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"docs/creating-skills.md","start_line":54,"end_line":61},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown guidance explicitly mandates a writing/language style requirement: descriptions 'MUST write in third person.' The policy scope includes natural-language constraints, and this requirement is presented as mandatory without offering author choice or a documented, region-specific justification.","remediation":"Relax the requirement to a recommendation, or document a clear organizational justification for the mandated style. If strict style is required, explain the rationale and scope so the constraint is clearly intentional and policy-compliant.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"docs/creating-skills.md","start_line":54,"end_line":61}]},{"id":"SC4","finding_id":"finding-c6e93378728e41c88f8fa8d80314ed96","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Known Vulnerable Dependency: esbuild==0.27.4 — 1 advisory(ies): GHSA-g7r4-m6w7-qqqr (esbuild allows arbitrary file read when running the development server on Window)","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"package-lock.json","start_line":762,"end_line":null},"finding":"esbuild==0.27.4","explanation":"Dependency has known vulnerabilities (CVEs). Using packages with unpatched security flaws exposes the environment to known exploits.","remediation":"Update the dependency to a patched version that addresses the known CVE. Check OSV (osv.dev) or NVD for details on the vulnerability.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"d8a8772a19f3743a04fa0ac6b93d74a1157e2436479cd0925c38306598f51879","occurrences":[{"file":"package-lock.json","start_line":762,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC1","finding_id":"finding-6bea0e8775624028a65ebbebdb8d6fd8","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unpinned Dependencies","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.4,"location":{"file":"package.json","start_line":13,"end_line":null},"finding":"\"tsx\": \"^4.20.5\"","explanation":"Dependencies lack version pinning, allowing potential malicious package updates. Consider pinning versions.","remediation":"Pin all dependency versions in requirements.txt or pyproject.toml. Use exact versions (==) or compatible ranges. Run pip-audit regularly.","code_snippet":"    \"test:coverage\": \"node --import tsx --experimental-test-coverage --test\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"tsx\": \"^4.20.5\"\n  }\n}","intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"5955d2dad55b7810d49be5d4866bfa92d622ec55c926a6af83b4cf411670eda3","occurrences":[{"file":"package.json","start_line":13,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-7d505e2b3a194d0c9a8a15073c872692","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"packages/baoyu-md/src/extensions/infographic.ts","start_line":77,"end_line":109},"finding":null,"explanation":"This code emits natural-language strings in Chinese for both the render failure message and the loading placeholder. That imposes a specific language on users without opt-in, which matches the language/locale policy violation criteria.","remediation":"Externalize user-facing strings and provide localization support or a user-selected language. If the skill is intentionally Chinese-only, document that locale restriction clearly and justify it in the skill description.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"packages/baoyu-md/src/extensions/infographic.ts","start_line":77,"end_line":109}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-9a7bf5bfa80e4c13886e56bb57b8716f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"packages/baoyu-md/src/extensions/markup.ts","start_line":4,"end_line":7},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file’s natural-language comments are written only in Chinese, which reflects a fixed language choice without any indication of user opt-in or a justified region-specific requirement. The policy explicitly asks to flag language or locale constraints when a specific language is forced without choice.","remediation":"Provide comments or user-facing text in the project’s standard language, add bilingual wording, or document that this skill/package is intentionally Chinese-specific and why that constraint is required.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"packages/baoyu-md/src/extensions/markup.ts","start_line":4,"end_line":7}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-c193c6b025184a37b0506399c63b2e82","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"packages/baoyu-md/src/extensions/plantuml.ts","start_line":181,"end_line":181},"finding":null,"explanation":"The loading message is presented only in Chinese, forcing a specific locale in the user-facing output. The file does not offer any configuration or opt-in for language selection, so this is a natural-language locale policy concern.","remediation":"Make user-facing messages configurable or localized, and provide a default that respects user/application language preferences rather than hardcoding Chinese text.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"packages/baoyu-md/src/extensions/plantuml.ts","start_line":181,"end_line":181}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-876f983039984ab381c